WHY A REWRITE, NOT A CONCEPT CHANGE
The only failing step is the "when" step "square six". Its kind of use is correct (an action step in the when block), but the operation named is squaring. The product document states: "The calculator offers one operation, Halve, which displays half the entered number. It has no Square operation." So squaring is not an item of the Public interface at all, and the existing concept "halve" ("Halve the entered number once.") must not be widened to admit it, nor may a new "square" concept be added for an operation the product does not offer. Everything else in the Story already describes halving: title "Halve a number", i_want "to halve a number", so_that "I can read its half", AC-1 "The number must be halved", given "six is entered", then "three is displayed" (three is half of six). The step text is the defect; the Story's intent is halving.

